# bat configuration (managed by chezmoi). One command-line argument per line.

# The token themes in themes/ are vendored from the neovim colorscheme's own
# extras (ThorstenRhau/token, contrib/bat), so `bat` matches the editor and the
# terminal. They are *not* built into bat: run_onchange_56_bat-cache runs
# `bat cache --build` at apply time, and without that both names below fail to
# resolve and bat falls back to its built-in default.
{{ if eq .chezmoi.os "darwin" -}}
# auto:system reads the macOS appearance directly — the same oracle dark-notify
# uses to drive `alacritty-theme auto`, so bat flips with everything else.
#
# Plain `auto` would ask the *terminal* for its background over OSC 11, and that
# query goes unanswered whenever output is redirected or tmux swallows it. It
# does not then fall back to --theme-dark; it falls back to bat's own default,
# so `bat file | cat` silently comes out Monokai. auto:system has no such hole,
# but it is macOS-only, hence the split.
--theme=auto:system
{{ else -}}
# auto:system is macOS-only, so Linux asks the terminal over OSC 11. Alacritty
# answers it, but a redirect or a tmux pane that eats the reply falls back to
# bat's built-in default rather than to --theme-dark below. If bat starts
# looking like Monokai in a pipeline, that is this — pass `--theme=dark` for the
# one-off, don't change this line.
--theme=auto
{{ end -}}
--theme-dark=token-dark
--theme-light=token-light
